  "raw": {
    "https://www.kettering.edu/co-op-career-design": {
      "title": "Co-op & Career Design",
      "description": "Co-op & Career Design | Kettering University Skip to main content kettering Toggle menu Academics + Research academics + research Academics + Research Overview Find Your Program Areas of Study Research Academic Affairs The Graduate School Global Engagement Academic Services Honors Program Corporate Partnerships Degrees + Programs Research Commencement Library Co-op Experience co-op experience Co-op Experience Overview Co-op Employer Partners Meet the Team Career Services Kettering Co-op vs. Internships Connect with a Co-op Manager Admissions + Aid admissions + aid Admissions & Aid Overview Financial Aid & Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Visit Graduate Admissions U.S. Military & Veterans International Students Meet Your Admissions Counselors Request Information Types of Aid Scholarships Life @ Kettering life @ kettering Life @ Kettering Overview Clubs & Organizations Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Campus Safety Parents & Families Competition Teams Campus Facilities Who We Are who we are Who We Are Overview Points of Pride News & Events Leadership Our History & Archives Campus Facilities Honorary Degrees Accreditation Policies Horsepower to Hyperloops Podcast Careers Media Resources Information For Parents + Families Alumni Community Robotics Request Info Apply Visit Give Toggle search Search Search Popular Searches Robotics Scholarships Co-op Experience Housing Clubs & Organizations Co-op & Career Design Accelerate your career before you even graduate. Kettering University’s immersive Co-op model helps you gain 2.5 years of paid, résumé-boosting experience that puts you miles ahead of your peers  — and they'll never catch up. Home / Co-op Experience Overview What are Co-ops? What are Co-ops? Kettering’s Co-op program is more than an internship. It's an immersive, no-holds-barred journey into the heart of your chosen field. In our unique 50/50 blend of rigorous academics and hands-on Co-op experience, you’ll spend one term mastering theories and skills in classrooms and labs and the next term applying them in your paid Co-op role. You won't just shadow professionals. You'll work alongside them, match their pace, and surpass their expectations. The results? You'll gain experience in a variety of areas. You'll earn $55,000 to $75,000+ over nine terms. And you'll develop the skills that could position you to bypass entry-level positions after graduation. Kettering Co-ops vs. Internships Kettering Co-op Highlights You might see other schools highlighting internship opportunities, but these don’t match up to the Co-ops you’ll take on at Kettering. View our Co-op Partners (PDF) # 1 Starting salaries in Michigan $ 75 , 700 Median starting salary of Kettering graduates, the highest in Michigan 11 weeks Our students work at their 11-week Co-op positions twice a year all four years at Kettering Student Coach & Employer Liaison Student Coach & Employer Liaison Student Coach and Employer Liaisons assist students starting before day one. Only Kettering has Student Coach and Employer Liaisons who connect with you immediately as you go through the enrollment process to set you up for success. Our Co-op team will help you find the best fit, perfect your résumé, and ace your interview. Connect With a Student Coach & Employer Liaison The Value of Your Co-op Experience “I get real-life experience as well as college experience, and it’s a nice 50/50. So I’m a completely hardworking engineer for half the year, and I’m a completely hardworking student for the other half.“ Aiden Grbic Engineering '24 Explore the B.S. in Engineering Explore the B.S. in Engineering “The thing that makes Kettering so unique and so beneficial to your future is coming out of college with work experience as well as the way that your brain interacts with learning and then doing.“ Samantha Kneebone Industrial Engineering '24 Explore the B.S. in Industrial Engineering Explore the B.S. in Industrial Engineering “The Co-op program allows us to maintain that balance of knowing what’s happening in the real world and how to implement it in the classroom and vice versa.“ Varun Rallabandi Computer Science '24 Explore the B.S. in Computer Science Explore the B.S. in Computer Science Career Sectors Kettering’s Co-op program empowers you to impact the most innovative industries, from automotive and robotics to artificial intelligence, biotech, and finance. Built for aspiring founders, directors, and CEOs, Kettering is where your leadership begins to take shape. Automotive Business Energy Technology Automotive Automotive Careers Kettering's pioneering research has shaped the automotive industry for over a century. Add to that legacy by driving the future of electric, autonomous transportation forward. Average Salary $102,810 Career Paths Automotive Engineer Crash Safety Engineer Mobility Systems Engineer New Product Development Co-op Employers by Industry (PDF) Programs Computer Engineering Electrical Engineering Industrial Engineering Mechanical Engineering Browse All Programs Co-op Employers American Axle Manufacturing Brose Ford Motor Company General Motors Co-op Employers by State (PDF) Business Business Careers Our business management degree programs offer industry-specific concentrations, and STEM-focused courses empower you to seize opportunities — and even create them. Average Salary $92,750 Career Paths Entrepreneurship Finance Marketing Supply Chain Management Co-op Employers by Industry (PDF) Programs Business (Management) Business Analytics Concentration Innovation and Entrepreneurship Concentration Supply Chain Management Certificate Browse All Programs Co-op Employers Divide by Design Joyson Safety Systems Lear Corporation Logofit Co-op Employers by State (PDF) Energy Energy Careers At Kettering, your curiosity will lead to solutions that make a tangible impact — from developing energy storage solutions to advancing electric transportation. The future starts with your next great idea, and you can find it here. Average Salary $112,100 Career Paths Environmental Engineer Fuel Cell Engineer Research Engineer Sustainability Engineer Co-op Partners by Industy (PDF) Programs Alternative Energy Concentration Chemical Engineering Industrial Engineering Manufacturing Systems Concentration Browse All Programs Co-op Employers BASF Corporation Dow Inc. Co-op Employers by State (PDF) Technology Technology Careers Transform hard-earned answers into real-world solutions with Kettering’s hands-on, practical learning approach. Here, you'll use the same computers, software, and hardware as professionals to create new products, streamline processes, and protect data. Average Salary $113,890 Career Paths AI Developer IT Security Analyst Software Engineer UX Designer Co-op Partners by Industry (PDF) Programs Artificial Intelligence Concentration Computer Engineering Computer Science Computer Gaming Concentration Browse All Programs Co-Op Employers Bosch Grid LLC Konrad Technologies Leidos Co-op Employers by State (PDF) Co-op Employer Partners Hundreds of companies seek out Kettering students each year for their entrepreneurial thinking and resilient mindset. These employers range from global corporations to local businesses across diverse fields, including robotics and healthcare. Full List of Active Employer Partners (PDF) How Does the Co-op Program Work? Use Kettering’s powerful network of employer partners and the guidance of our Coach and Employer Liaisons to find positions that build the connections and experience you need to jump-start your career. Average Completion Time 4.5 to 5 Years Work Experience 2.5 Years Attending School Starting your first year, you’ll spend three months in the classroom and three months at your Co-op. This rotation of classroom and Co-op continues throughout your time at Kettering, allowing you to apply what you learn to real-world situations immediately and bring back industry best practices. Working at Your Co-op At your Co-op, you will: Meet deadlines and work like a pro: Gain practical experience in time management and teamwork. Reap industry insights: Learn directly from current employers and provide valuable input based on your coursework. Impress employers: Make first -- and lasting -- impressions with focus and efficiency, showcasing your professional skills. Lead teams: Potentially oversee a team of employees, preparing you for leadership roles before you even graduate. Essential Skills The Co-op program at Kettering equips you for career success in any field. You'll hone your technical expertise, sharpen critical thinking, enhance communication, master time management, and excel in teamwork. Co-op is an invaluable experience, laying a solid foundation for your future career and setting you apart in the professional world. Career Design Immersing yourself in a professional workplace lets you experience your potential career path firsthand. Discover your passion for your department and explore similar roles that interest you even more. The Co-op program offers the flexibility to pivot if you change your major or concentration or simply want diverse industry experiences. It's your gateway to real-world insight and adaptability in your career journey. Keep Exploring Kettering Have the career preparation you need to be at the forefront of innovation with Kettering University’s Co-op program. Achieve greater and arrive faster — starting now. Request Info Visit Apply kettering 810-762-9500 1700 University Ave., Flint MI 48504 Students Campus Safety Spirit Store Kettering News Library Visitors Faculty Directory Careers Social Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube X Contact Us Directions to Campus My Kettering Acceptable Use Policy Consumer Information Financial Information Privacy Title IX © 2024 Kettering University. All Rights Reserved"
    },
