      "description": "Career Services | Kettering University Skip to main content kettering Toggle menu Academics + Research academics + research Academics + Research Overview Find Your Program Areas of Study Research Academic Affairs The Graduate School Global Engagement Academic Services Honors Program Corporate Partnerships Degrees + Programs Research Commencement Library Co-op Experience co-op experience Co-op Experience Overview Co-op Employer Partners Meet the Team Career Services Kettering Co-op vs. Internships Connect with a Co-op Manager Admissions + Aid admissions + aid Admissions & Aid Overview Financial Aid & Affordability Undergraduate Admissions Visit Graduate Admissions U.S. Military & Veterans International Students Meet Your Admissions Counselors Request Information Types of Aid Scholarships Life @ Kettering life @ kettering Life @ Kettering Overview Clubs & Organizations Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Campus Safety Parents & Families Competition Teams Campus Facilities Who We Are who we are Who We Are Overview Points of Pride News & Events Leadership Our History & Archives Campus Facilities Honorary Degrees Accreditation Policies Horsepower to Hyperloops Podcast Careers Media Resources Information For Parents + Families Alumni Community Robotics Request Info Apply Visit Give Toggle search Search Search Popular Searches Robotics Scholarships Co-op Experience Housing Clubs & Organizations Career Services Home / Co-op Experience Overview / Career Services Co-op Experience Overview Menu Career Services Co-op Employer Partners Meet the Team Ella Derricks Karen Owens Michael Cooper Neil Richey Riley Boomgaard Sarah Perkins Co-ops vs Internships Bulldog Career Services Login Employer Login Android Handshake App Apple Handshake App Career Services Kettering University’s Co-op & Career Design connects graduating undergraduate seniors, graduate students, and alumni with potential employers through various opportunities, including access to all employment and career fairs, networking events, and company spotlight days hosted by Kettering. Students and alumni can also benefit from complimentary on-campus mock interviews and resume reviews, access to career platforms powered by Handshake. Students and alumni can quickly introduce themselves to Kettering-approved employers by creating rich profiles in the Handshake platform that gets them noticed. Jobs relevant to the user can be easily filtered with the ability to apply instantly. Using Handshake - Students and Alumni Students can access Bulldog Career Services by visiting handshake.kettering.edu or by downloading the Handshake app for any Apple or Android device. Alumni can create an account on Handshake by visiting joinhandshake.com. Click on sign-up and follow the prompts using a personal email address. If you are experiencing technical difficulties please send an email to itapps@kettering.edu . Using Handshake - Employers Handshake allows you to recruit the highly skilled graduates of Kettering University. To get started on the platform visit joinhandshake.com . kettering 810-762-9500 1700 University Ave., Flint MI 48504 Students Campus Safety Spirit Store Kettering News Library Visitors Faculty Directory Careers Social Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube X Contact Us Directions to Campus My Kettering Acceptable Use Policy Consumer Information Financial Information Privacy Title IX © 2024 Kettering University. All Rights Reserved"
